{"source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "hash": "9a0566086e409a7176d212dc49ff4b32181906a521977d75389f2b924680a91b", "nodes": [{"id": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_doc", "label": "State doc 2026-06-25: artefact tag-facets vs routing (the re-split) — the current facet baseline, crystallized from the 06-15/16 session; supersedes the 06-14 relevance-channels framing.", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_the_cut", "label": "The cut (user-decided): separate tag-facets from routing — tag-facets = a semantic description of the phrase (v1's concept, no numbers); routing = a separate downstream job that consumes facets and owns relevance/weighting.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_facet_not_coordinate", "label": "A tag-facet is a dimension of MEANING read off the phrase, NOT a 'relevance coordinate' — the relevance-coordinate framing (06-14) was routing leaking into the facet definition and is dead.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_v2_interpreter_flavoured", "label": "The v2 five (stance/function/temporal-stance especially) read as interpreter/query-decomposition axes; v1's facets were the tag's actual semantic meaning 'around the tag'.", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_hollowed_tag", "label": "The v2 single-phrase tag is 'hollowed out' (semantics shipped to structure); the facet CONCEPT (not the weighting) returns as a semantic layer on the v2 phrases.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_corpus_relative", "label": "Per-facet value is corpus-relative (IDF-like) over the whole tag-corpus, stored as a small facet-vector ATTRIBUTE on the tag — never nodes/edges (too heavy), model emits nothing; calibration, not axis-definition.", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_topic_is_centrality", "label": "Topic is not a facet (the phrase IS the topic); topic-as-degree = the tag's centrality within its chunk, measured against its sibling tags (chunk-local reference frame).", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_set_reopened", "label": "OPEN: the tag-facet SET (which dimensions are tag-native vs interpreter/routing-side) and how each facet axis is DEFINED (corpus-relativity calibrates a tag along an axis but does not define the axis).", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_the_cut", "target": "state_2026_06_25_tfvr_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "state/2026-06-25-artefact-tag-facets-vs-routing.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "